Primary prior defect is remediated in the final working tree:
  Must-have "Scale reserved-head similarity by candidate length" is implemented.
  decorationTagFinding → nearest(..., (candidate) => candidate.length <= 5 ? 1 : 2)
  nearest() accepts number | ((candidate: string) => number) and skips candidates
  outside their per-candidate max before unique-winner selection.

Behavioral proof (code + tests + harness):
  - Short reserved heads (≤5: kind/pack/spec): d=1 only
      kindle ↛ kind (d=2) inert; paced ↛ pack (d=2) inert
      king → kind (d=1); packs → pack (d=1) refuse without illegal did-you-mean
  - Long reserved heads (>5): d≤2
      readines → readiness (d=1)
      constraind-by → constrained-by (d=1)
      constraind-bi → constrained-by (d=2)  [explicit two-edit test]
      example-spac → example-space (d=1)
  - Tests green: gherkin-reifier 58 + gherkin-parity 5 = 63 passed
  - No plan deviation / no missing trade-off record required (behavior matches Must-have)

Note (non-blocking): one test title still says "length ≤5 one-edit near miss" while
